{
  "title": "ISic002136. Funerary epitaph for Agathopous",
  "body": "<div id=\"editions\"><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: <a href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/4MCP2PVV\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/4MCP2PVV</a></div><div id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  <div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  <a id=\"al1-interpretive\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Ἀγαθόπο\n                    υς\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἀγαθόπο\n                    υς\">Ἀγαθόπο-<br id=\"al2-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span>υς</span></span> χρη-<br id=\"al3-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span>στὸς καὶ <br id=\"al4-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span>[ἄμεμ]πτος <br id=\"al5-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span><span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>  <br id=\"al6-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">6</span><span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>  </span></div>  <p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: <a href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/4MCP2PVV\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/4MCP2PVV</a></div><div id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\"><div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\"><a id=\"al1-diplomatic\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Ἀγαθόπο\n                    υς\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἀγαθόπο\n                    υς\">ΑΓΑΘΟΠΟ<br id=\"al2-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span>ΥΣ</span></span>ΧΡΗ<br id=\"al3-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span>ΣΤΟΣΚΑΙ<br id=\"al4-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span>[....]ΠΤΟΣ<br id=\"al5-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span><span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span><br id=\"al6-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">6</span><span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span></span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div></div>  <div id=\"facsimile-images\"><h2>Facsimile Images</h2></div>  <div id=\"apparatus\"><h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span><span>Text after Orsi 1912 and a low resolution photograph; fresh study is required</span></span>; </li><li><span class=\"2\">2: <span>It is clear that the text in line 2 is complete, and the name carries over from line 1 to 2, for the more common form Ἀγαθόπους; this further implies that the damage on the right is ancient, preceding inscription.</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"5\">5: <span>The traces are clearly compatible with some version of ἔζησεν ἔτη</span></span></li></ul></div>  <div id=\"translation\"><h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537\">Jonathan Prag</a></p>  <p>Agathopous, worthy and blameless [lived...].</p>  </div>  <div id=\"commentary\"><h2>commentary</h2>  <p>  </p></div>  <div id=\"bibliography\"><h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> Orsi NSA 1912 299 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001392\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001392</a>  </li></ul>  <ul><li></li></ul>  </div>  <div id=\"handnote\"><p>Regular plain letters, lunate sigma and epsilon</p> Line 1    Interlineation line 1 to 2    </div><div id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. </div>",
